26. Test Implementation Rules

Tests must verify observable business outcomes.

Avoid tests that only prove:

method X was called

Prefer tests that prove:

business state changed correctly
database state is correct
message was produced correctly
output was generated correctly
duplicate processing did not occur
failure recovered correctly

Use deterministic test data.

Do not introduce flaky sleeps where a deterministic synchronization mechanism can be used.

