41. Important Engineering Rules

Follow these rules throughout the work:

1. Do not assume requirements are implemented. Verify them.
2. Do not assume tests prove business behavior. Inspect what they actually assert.
3. Do not modify code before understanding the workflow.
4. Do not fabricate test or build results.
5. Do not disable tests to make the build pass.
6. Do not silently change business requirements.
7. Do not make unnecessary architectural changes.
8. Do not leave implementation/documentation inconsistent.
9. Do not introduce unbounded concurrency.
10. Do not introduce unsafe retry behavior.
11. Do not assume exactly-once processing. Design for idempotency.
12. Do not rely on in-memory state for durable business processing.
13. Do not expose secrets or sensitive business data in logs/tests.
14. Do not mark a requirement complete without executable evidence where testing is feasible.
15. Do not report success when the environment prevented validation.

